#Donor/acceptor classification for the dynamic hydrogen-bond mechanism.
#
#Format: <resname> <type> <donor> <acceptor> [<antecedent> [[~|^]<second>[:angle]]]
#
#ATOMS ARE NAMED BY THEIR GROUP, which is the first column of the .grp -- AN for
#alanine's backbone nitrogen, ACA for its alpha carbon. That is the name the
#topology carries once it has been reduced, so there is ONE convention and
#nothing to translate: no .grp to restate in the .msp, no second copy of this
#table in another spelling, and no guessing.
#
#The one exception is a CROSS-RESIDUE antecedent, '-C' or '+P', which cannot be
#a group name: the type of an atom in the neighbouring residue depends on which
#residue that is. Those are written as plain atom names, and pdb2spn records
#what its .grp renamed so that they resolve exactly -- see
#spn::Particle::getOriginalName.
#
#Companion to RNAAtomRigidGroups.rbody and RNAAtomTorsion.bi.ff, and named
#like them. Kept separate from the protein and DNA tables on purpose.
#
#The classification is not invented here: it follows HBPLUS (McDonald &
#Thornton) and Reduce/Probe, and the files it replaces carried it unchanged.

A    rOP1   0 2 rP
RA   rOP1   0 2 rP
A    rOP2   0 2 rP
RA   rOP2   0 2 rP
A    rO5    0 2 rC5   rP
RA   rO5    0 2 rC5   rP
A    rO4    0 2 rC4   1C1
RA   rO4    0 2 rC4   1C1
A    aN7    0 1 aC5   aC8
RA   aN7    0 1 aC5   aC8
A    aN6    2 0 aC6   ~aN1
RA   aN6    2 0 aC6
A    aN1    0 1 aC2   aC6
RA   aN1    0 1 aC2   aC6
A    aN3    0 1 aC2   aC4
RA   aN3    0 1 aC2   aC4
A    rO2    1 2 rC2
RA   rO2    1 2 rC2
A    rO3    0 2 rC3   +P
RA   rO3    0 2 rC3   +P
C    rOP1   0 2 rP
RC   rOP1   0 2 rP
C    rOP2   0 2 rP
RC   rOP2   0 2 rP
C    rO5    0 2 rC5   rP
RC   rO5    0 2 rC5   rP
C    rO4    0 2 rC4   2C1
RC   rO4    0 2 rC4   2C1
C    cN4    2 0 cC4   ~cN3
RC   cN4    2 0 cC4
C    cN3    0 1 cC2   cC4
RC   cN3    0 1 cC2   cC4
C    cO2    0 2 cC2   ~cN3
RC   cO2    0 2 cC2
C    rO2    1 2 rC2
RC   rO2    1 2 rC2
C    rO3    0 2 rC3   +P
RC   rO3    0 2 rC3   +P
G    rOP1   0 2 rP
RG   rOP1   0 2 rP
G    rOP2   0 2 rP
RG   rOP2   0 2 rP
G    rO5    0 2 rC5   rP
RG   rO5    0 2 rC5   rP
G    rO4    0 2 rC4   3C1
RG   rO4    0 2 rC4   3C1
G    gN7    0 1 gC5   gC8
RG   gN7    0 1 gC5   gC8
G    gO6    0 2 gC6   ~gN1
RG   gO6    0 2 gC6
G    gN1    1 0 gC2   gC6
RG   gN1    1 0 gC2   gC6
G    gN2    2 0 gC2   ~gN1
RG   gN2    2 0 gC2
G    gN3    0 1 gC2   gC4
RG   gN3    0 1 gC2   gC4
G    rO2    1 2 rC2
RG   rO2    1 2 rC2
G    rO3    0 2 rC3   +P
RG   rO3    0 2 rC3   +P
U    rOP1   0 2 rP
RU   rOP1   0 2 rP
U    rOP2   0 2 rP
RU   rOP2   0 2 rP
U    rO5    0 2 rC5   rP
RU   rO5    0 2 rC5   rP
U    rO4    0 2 rC4   4C1
RU   rO4    0 2 rC4   4C1
U    uO4    0 2 uC4   ~uN3
RU   uO4    0 2 uC4
U    uN3    1 0 uC2   uC4
RU   uN3    1 0 uC2   uC4
U    uO2    0 2 uC2
RU   uO2    0 2 uC2
U    rO2    1 2 rC2
RU   rO2    1 2 rC2
U    rO3    0 2 rC3   +P
RU   rO3    0 2 rC3   +P
